    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on our elite speed-and-power hybrids at the top of the order. **Trea Turner** (78.26) is our strongest start of the day, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Sugano and a prime leadoff spot that maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our Roto strategy. He is closely shadowed by **Kyle Schwarber** (74.74) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28), who remain locked in our outfield despite the threat of tough left-handed starters. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces the left-handed Abbott, his elite 0.428 xwOBA makes him an auto-start regardless of platoon splits. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Junior Caminero** (63.50); despite a difficult matchup against Tolle, his high base projection and spot in the two-hole make him a high-efficiency utility play.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal 40-59 range, where we ultimately chose to bench **Chase Meidroth** (37.95) in favor of keeping the floor high. **Chase Meidroth** struggled to clear the threshold due to a daunting matchup against Gilbert, whose 3.09 xERA significantly suppressed the projection. We continue to monitor **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12), who remains active despite the heavy risk of facing the elite deGrom; while his defensive and speed utility is vital to the Zebras, the negative SP skill impact is a flashing red light for his ceiling today. \n\nStrategic risks are prevalent throughout today\u2019s lineup. We are closely tracking the status of **Dillon Dingler** (62.05), who benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage against Cameron, though his lower base projection leaves little margin for error. We have ruled out **Colt Keith** as he is not in the confirmed lineup, and we continue to wait for **Christian Yelich** and **Zac Veen** to return from their respective IL and minor league assignments. As a reminder, any late-breaking lineup changes regarding **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Carson Benge**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, or **Luis Pena** will be processed through our bench utility to ensure we stay above the daily game cap efficiency floor.",
